  "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-1.2<Z<-0.31).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/46b71217fcee1d130b3778ce2cd101aac9814870b71683656987d476e71412c1.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=\u03a6(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\u03a6(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.2<Z<-0.31) & =P(Z<-0.31)-P(Z\\le -1.2) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.31)-P(Z\\le -1.2) \\\\  & =\u03a6(-0.31)-\u03a6(-1.2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(-1.2) & =0.1151 \\\\ \u03a6(-0.31) & =0.3783\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.2<Z<-0.31) & =\u03a6(-0.31)-\u03a6(-1.2) \\\\  & =0.3783-0.1151 \\\\  & =0.2632.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
